<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.1.13.2.1"/>
    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Attacks of breathlessness and wheeze, the worst last night, two days after returning from the mountains. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Swami Vivekananda returned two days ago from seven months of travel in the mountains. He was well in the dry, cool hills. For about three weeks, since coming down to the damp plains, he has had attacks of wheeze, cough and tightness lasting hours, mostly at night, and last night he sat up for most of the night feeling that he was suffocating. Smoke from the kitchen fires and incense make it worse. He has never had asthma diagnosed and has no inhaler. He has no fever, chest pain, ankle swelling or orthopnea between attacks, and no green sputum. He has taken metformin 1872 mg, losartan and atorvastatin throughout his travels; his fasting readings were 110 to 135 mg/dL, and 196 mg/dL this morning after a sleepless night. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Three weeks, since coming down to the plains; worst last night</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Sat up most of the night; speaks in sentences today; peak flow 330 L/min</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Type 2 diabetes on metformin; no previous asthma diagnosis or inhaler</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Night cough; no fever, chest pain, edema or purulent sputum</td></tr><tr><td>Glucose</td><td>Fasting 110 to 135 mg/dL while travelling; 196 mg/dL this morning</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

