    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1898-10-20; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Tired, sitting upright, speaking in full sentences; mild use of the neck muscles</td></tr><tr><td>Vital signs</td><td>Pulse 108, respiratory rate 24, oxygen saturation 94 percent on room air, temperature 36.9 °C; peak flow 330 L/min (56 percent of predicted)</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Widespread expiratory wheeze with fair air entry; no crackles</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Tachycardic, regular; jugular venous pressure not raised; no edema</td></tr><tr><td>Reassessment after one hour</td><td>After albuterol 4 puffs by spacer three times over an hour: peak flow 410 L/min (69 percent, a rise of 24 percent), oxygen saturation 96 percent, pulse 98, wheeze much reduced</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

